// D1565 — THREE `__array_new_default__` holes linked in a CHAIN. D1512 gave the two defaulting
// sites one shared pin point that consults the link; the consult was ONE HOP, and
// `flushUninferred` walks pending bindings in DECLARATION order, so the first hole is asked
// before the second has resolved, finds its partner open, and takes `i32` while the rest of the
// chain lands on `f64`.
//
// THE DELIVERY IS THE CHAIN'S LAST ROW, not a fourth link: `const v = __h3` binds `v` to
// `__h3`'s own row (`noteHoleLink` declines `a == b`), so the pin the proof applies lands on
// the end of a three-row chain — the D1512 residue's exact shape at every position. The
// ANNOTATED face is the control: an annotation pins at `constrainEmptyD`'s OTHER arm, which
// resolves each row in place as the chain is walked and needs no link at all.
//
// The proof STORES before it reads, for `array-new-default-f64.matrix.vl`'s reason: every slot
// `array.new_default` writes is a zero, and `0` reads the same off the i32 backing as off the
// f64 one.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@SKIP@@
argument: an un-annotated PARAM is a `TyVar` — it pins nothing and links nothing (D1471)
// @@SETUP@@
let __h1 = __array_new_default__(3)
let __h2 = __array_new_default__(3)
let __h3 = __array_new_default__(3)
__h2 = __h1
__h3 = __h2
// @@VALUE@@
__h3
// @@TYPE@@
f64[]
// @@PROOF@@
v[0] = 1.25
print(v[0] + 0.25)
// @@WANT@@
1.5
